WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.937
Repeated internal whitespace requires a pattern-based solution.

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:10.527
The PostgreSQL regular-expression pattern bracket colon space colon bracket represents whitespace.

00:00:10.527 --> 00:00:13.297
The plus means one or more occurrences.

00:00:13.297 --> 00:00:19.442
Replacing that run with one ordinary space turns values with inconsistent spacing into a more stable

00:00:19.442 --> 00:00:26.152
representation. We usually trim boundaries first and then normalize the internal whitespace.

00:00:26.152 --> 00:00:30.127
Text cleaning should separate normalization from interpretation.

00:00:30.127 --> 00:00:35.562
Trimming spaces or standardizing case is usually safe when the rule is documented;

00:00:35.562 --> 00:00:40.702
correcting a person's name or guessing an email address is a much stronger intervention.

00:00:40.702 --> 00:00:43.948
Preserve the original value when auditability matters.
